---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { GITHUB_REPO_URL, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const description =
	"About this sample: a custom blog built and deployed end to end.";
---

<Layout title={`About - ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={description}>
	<h1>About</h1>
	<p>
		This is a custom blog built with Astro, Payload CMS, and SQLite. It 
		showcases a real, end-to-end integration of these technologies. It 
		features an admin dashboard for managing content, including creating, 
		editing, and deleting posts with tags, drafts, richtext editing and 
		media uploads.
	</p>
	<p>
		While the admin dashboard handles managing content, this front-end uses
		Astro to render extremely fast and optimized static pages. Both are 
		deployed to a single serverless compute instance behind a reverse proxy.
		The SQLite database is used to store CMS data and is replicated to Google
		Cloud Storage for a cheap, minimal persistence layer.
	</p>
	<h2>Not a real publication</h2>
	<p>
		If you're looking at this expecting a real publication - it isn't one -
		it merely exists to showcase integration of these technologies and
		the real GCP infrastructure behind it.
	</p>
</Layout>
